    {
      "id": "claim_180d39905b1c404d8f01890a915c0e15",
      "statement": "QEMU's 10.0.2.2 host alias works for TCP from the emulator on this machine; the earlier claim that it was broken was refuted with a negative control on 2026-08-23. The real rule is per-service: an RN 0.85 debug build resolves Metro to 10.0.2.2:8081 and does not consult adb reverse tcp:8081 for the bundle fetch, while Keycloak and the BFF must be reached at localhost through adb reverse tcp:8082 and tcp:8099, re-established after every emulator restart.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.forgejo/workflows/app-ci.yml#L413-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15636d748427b67b34bd73013c8a077e4545d5995bd442e26a8c99bd231fc19d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/android-emulator.md#L125-L181",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe8e398ec762fed3af04c60bca180cc32440f3ea1d032159c550830c0db321c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3786eebdb5204368ad4a56feca176f4f",
      "statement": "Keycloak is pinned with KC_HOSTNAME=http://localhost:8099, so it issues its issuer and session cookies for localhost; reaching the same server at 10.0.2.2:8099 loses the cookies and login dies mid-flow with cookie_not_found and an app-side no-code-param abort. CI bakes localhost URLs and tunnels both ports for exactly this reason.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.forgejo/workflows/app-ci.yml#L413-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15636d748427b67b34bd73013c8a077e4545d5995bd442e26a8c99bd231fc19d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/android-emulator.md#L160-L169",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d53ee493e6c396ba10a0fc70b157a1ce4db1b168029f2c60dacdf10e12a5e60f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a01ded1128564f29a3eba8ad42dbfe47",
      "statement": "If something else already holds host port 8081 (a stale VS Code dev-container forward is the common case), the app hangs on the splash screen forever with no redbox and no error because the handshake succeeds and no response arrives; diagnosis is to identify the listener's owning process rather than to test reachability.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/android-emulator.md#L149-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:810065447729f10525556c74ac3dadd2115370cd55ca35fb9504884adf2d943e:"
        }
