          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f47727263cd7bf6e9eed0c48edfb7d89fbdee94de21ee703e7994cb655db80e5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_456270ccd69f44c1832d9f032ecaad5c",
      "statement": "Two emulator-state conditions mimic app bugs: a second installed MCM build (any bundle id) also claims the shared mcm-app:// OAuth scheme, so Android shows an unanswerable Open-with chooser mid-login and the flow times out; and a live Chrome Keycloak SSO session makes the next login submission fail with already_logged_in and redirect back with no code, which scripts/ci-mobile-agent-flows.sh clears via adb shell pm clear com.android.chrome.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/android-emulator.md#L182-L193",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:774b854a5e7bca5908311a38431113fab68ac97bccce9d758bebff184cf16688:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/ci-mobile-agent-flows.sh#L160-L177",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67e3a03fa0ccc186abca5d1db9ae879984c4be06696d12831bc08a4a1795a765:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ad2e1f7c7de647d9bc633a3cd048823b",
      "statement": "app-e2e verifies /dev/kvm is present in the job container and exits 1 with an ::error:: naming the runner-config fix if it is not, rather than letting the mobile suite skip silently; /dev/kvm is provided by the runner config's `container.options: --device /dev/kvm` (plus the ci user's kvm group membership), not by a udev rule, because the GitHub-host-VM approach does not apply inside a container.",
      "evidence": [
